{"id": "EUVD-2026-48866", "enisaUuid": "4e0b4cda-5b3d-3053-b516-e73309ce9842", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5e: Fix eswitch mode block underflow on IPsec acquire SA\n\nmlx5e_xfrm_add_state() handles acquire-flow temporary SAs by allocating\nsoftware state and skipping hardware offload setup.\n\nThat path jumps to the common success label before taking the eswitch mode\nblock. After tunnel-mode validation was moved earlier, the common success\nlabel unconditionally calls mlx5_eswitch_unblock_mode(). For acquire SAs,\nthis decrements esw->offloads.num_block_mode without a matching increment.\n\nReturn directly after installing the acquire SA offload handle, so only the\npaths that successfully called mlx5_eswitch_block_mode() call the matching\nunblock.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T09:14:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:37", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5bd4249e430f5963d559708ee96a671716d2400", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ecafd8284e527666e83261e6e57a7c7341d591cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abe003b33223ff33552f291644bf35d9c2f992fb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64522", "GHSA-x5f7-rh4c-gxvr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.51, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1fd0dbd1-9d9c-376f-a4c2-c7bab4193faa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "993c4ba71596c30418ba5a0ddcf4f9c2f431466a"}, {"id": "22a4ff6c-4c80-3779-a88b-8885d843020f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3174101f-5778-3db0-b819-8a7b4e5782a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "35552796-7eb3-3bf2-a554-8d27dd20ff82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22239eb258bc1e6ccdb2d3502fce1cc2b2a88386 <ecafd8284e527666e83261e6e57a7c7341d591cb"}, {"id": "4669b550-f8e1-3e29-b1b5-848fcc3f19fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22239eb258bc1e6ccdb2d3502fce1cc2b2a88386 <abe003b33223ff33552f291644bf35d9c2f992fb"}, {"id": "5a96bcce-ad6c-37ce-b4ef-ed30f0a2d983", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22239eb258bc1e6ccdb2d3502fce1cc2b2a88386 <b5bd4249e430f5963d559708ee96a671716d2400"}, {"id": "9a0e53f1-02e5-3932-9329-77eab71ebeb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.34"}, {"id": "b3d484b8-463c-3f20-ad48-4f73af576a06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "c7a2df1a-0d77-3eb9-9855-a0794eb6f3b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17.4 <6.18"}, {"id": "fdaafa46-4a82-31e2-a883-e3e0b4d11e9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fabfdf23-e556-394a-9cf1-a6d2526464c3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}